 # Differentiable and inverse volume rendering
 ## Overview
-This family encompasses methods that treat volume rendering as a differentiable operation to solve inverse problems, optimizing 3D scene representations from 2D observations without requiring 3D ground truth supervision [43-differentiable-volume-rendering.md]. It sets itself apart from [Radiance-field optimization](44-radiance-field-optimization.md) by focusing on the general differentiability of the volume rendering integral rather than specific neural field architectures, and from [Tomographic reconstruction as inverse rendering](45-tomographic-reconstruction-as-inverse-rendering.md) by encompassing both tomographic and non-tomographic (e.g., RGB-only) optimization loops [43-differentiable-volume-rendering.md].
